# WRONG on purpose (panel 177's critic, `cb_return_poison64`; item 1's
# *callback results*). On one path the callback gives its node back and then
# returns the same BINDING to C, which writes 64 bytes into it. The poison
# prototyped at the sitting emptied `m` and nothing checked the RESULT of a
# callback, so C wrote through the dead value into the runtime's own statics,
# exit 0 on three legs, `--sanitize` silent where the base compiler's had
# said `heap-use-after-free`. The thunk C is handed checks every handle the
# result reaches before returning it (`emit/callback_thunk.hero`), and the
# dead value is an address on a page nobody can write. The path depends on
# the value C passes, which the checker's half (item 3) cannot decide.

extern "dead-handle-returned-by-a-callback-is-checked.h"
    record Node tag node
    function node_new() -> Node acquires node_free
    function node_free(n: Node consumes)
    function ask(cb: (function(i32) -> Node)) -> i64

function give(k: i32) -> Node
    m: Node @ node_new()

    if k > 2
        node_free(n: m)
    return m

function main()
    print("C wrote ", ask(cb: give))
